  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1022 PM CDT Thu Jul 30 2026\n\nModels depict the upper wave currently over the central Plains\nmoving towards the central Appalachians, cutting off from the main\nflow, and retrograding. This will act to slow the broader pattern\nevolution. Hot and primarily dry conditions remain the \nexpectation for next week, as the upper ridge becomes flattened \nbut keeps above normal heights in place over W TX. The ensemble \nmean 500mb height forecast is generally between 592-596 dam next \nweek. Ensemble guidance continues to highlight a good chance \n(50-80%) for daily high temperatures above 100 degrees off the \nCaprock, with lower chances (10-30%) for reaching such values on \nthe Caprock. It remains to be seen if the ridge flattens enough \nthat disturbances rounding it track close enough to clip the \nforecast area with precip. For now, the NBM keeps the forecast \narea dry, with PoPs less than 10% each day Sunday onward.",
